# Database safety

## Production / MAIN game DB — read-only (absolute)

- No AI writes, merges, DDL, DML, migrations, or schema push on MAIN / production game DB.
- Ordinary reads: `MIRROR_PRODUCTION_DB` / `MIRROR_DEV_DB` (fail closed, read-only).
- Do not build features that require a MAIN schema change — model in ADMIN or say it can't ship.
- Missing MAIN indexes: document in `prisma/recommended-indexes.sql` only; never apply on primary.

## Admin DB — full access

- Reviewed idempotent SQL under `drizzle/admin/migrations/`.
- Apply with `npm run admin:sql -- <file>`, then `npm run db:pull:admin`.
- Audit-log admin mutations via `createAdminAuditEvent()`.

## Antifraud DB — full access

- Full task-scoped DDL/DML/migrations/ops allowed after verifying target + impact.
- Keep MAIN game DB out of antifraud mutation paths.

## Secrets

Local `.env` points at live prod. Never commit, print, log, or paste `DATABASE_URL` or derived secrets.

## Query rules

- Every MAIN read hits a confirmed index, or has an `EXPLAIN ANALYZE` reason.
- Drizzle by default; parameterized `sql` only — never concatenate user input.
- Lists paginate server-side. Heavy pages: shell-first `PageHero` + `<Suspense>` + matching `loading.tsx`.
- Active timeframe/tab only — don't prefetch every window/tab.
- Money is `Decimal(20,2)` — no JS float math. Reuse existing GGR/NGR/P&L queries.
